    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50594" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰόμωροι</span></b> , οἱ, twice in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργεῖοι ἰόμωροι, ἐλεγχέες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.242
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργεῖοι ἰόμωροι, ἀπειλάων ἀκόρητοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.479
				</span></i>
			. (Expld. by Sch. as <i>caring for arrows</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέριμνα</span>), but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span> is against this: perh. <i>noisy</i>
			(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰά</span>).)</div>
